WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.125
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN: Heads up.

00:00:01.125 --> 00:00:02.700
LORIN PRICE: Whoa.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.290
Easy there.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.230
Not everyone has time for
these fun beach antics.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.450
I have a network to maintain.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.759
Gotta make sure these
developers play by the rules.

00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:13.800
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN: Why are
you worried about that?

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.720
Aren't you using Shared VPC?

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.630
LORIN PRICE: What's Shared VPC?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:19.830
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN: Shared
VPC allows an organization

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.400
to connect resources
from multiple projects

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.320
to a common VPC network so
that they can communicate

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.840
with each other securely
and efficiently,

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.390
use internal IPs
from that network.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.250
LORIN PRICE: Wow.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.000
But how does that help
me with maintaining

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.362
control of my network?

00:00:34.362 --> 00:00:35.820
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN:
Shared VPC admins

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.610
can delegate network
administration tasks

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.909
to network and security admins
in the Shared VPC network.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:43.200
LORIN PRICE: Now we're talking.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.670
Can you show me
how to set it up?

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.090
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN: You bet.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:45.870
Let's take a look.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:56.000
To start off, I'm logged
in as Gustavo Mantovan,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.890
with the organizational
administrator for this domain,

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.440
bringtothecloud.com.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.070
After I'm logged in,
the organization admin

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:10.330
needs to elect someone
or a group of people

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.510
to be the compute
Shared VPC admin

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.240
on the organizational
level, who in this case

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:18.190
will be Mary Smith.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:20.890
Normally, it will be whoever
is responsible for managing

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.420
the network in your environment.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.190
We will also give the
project owner permission

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.430
to Mary for the Shared
VPC host project.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.400
So she can create new
VPCs and firewalls.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.310
This is not a required
step to set up Shared VPC.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.190
However for this demo
it will make it easier

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:44.245
to demonstrate the
Shared VPC creation.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:52.000
Once that's done, I'll log
out as Gustavo there on admin,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.750
and I will login as Mary
with the Shared VPC admin

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:58.140
and can set up the Shared VPC.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.490
After I'm logged
in as Mary, I will

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:04.990
go to the
bttc-sharedvpc-hostproject,

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:08.150
which will be the host
project for the Shared VPC.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:13.000
And for this demo, I
will create a new VPC

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.290
called
sharedvpc-bringtothecloud,

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:21.250
with two subnetworks,
one for development

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.960
and another for production.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.380
Mary, as the net ops
engineer, does not

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.920
want anyone to be using
the default VPC on the host

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.180
project.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:35.530
So she deleted the G4 VPC.

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:39.280
Once that's complete, Mary
creates two firewalls,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.500
one for allowing SSH to
the instance in the new VPC

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:47.890
and another allowing ICMP
between the two subnetworks.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.900
This rule we are
creating just to show

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.140
we have connectivity between
different subnetworks

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.582
within the Shared VPC.

00:02:54.582 --> 00:02:57.220
Now that Mary has everything
set up and ready to go,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.660
she will go ahead and start
creating the Shared VPC.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.870
She goes to the Shared VPC page
and clicks Set Up Shared VPC.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.340
First step is to enable
these projects as the host

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.530
projects of the Shared VPC.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:10.600
Next, you'll have
to select which

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:14.530
subnets you want to
share in the Shared VPC.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:17.530
You can select all subnets
or select individual.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.590
In this case, Mary selects
the development and production

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.880
subnets.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.370
Finally, you have to select
the projects you want

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.160
to attach to the Shared VPC.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.860
Those projects are
called service projects,

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.110
and they will consume the
networks from the host project.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:38.090
Mary selects the development
and the production projects.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:40.560
After doing that, I
will logout as Mary

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:43.730
and login as Charko,
the development owner,

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:47.165
and create an instance
using the Shared VPC subnet.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:57.620
As you can see, Charko checks
the box Networks Shared With Me

00:03:57.620 --> 00:03:59.190
and select the
Development subnet.

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:07.940
After that, he creates
the instance normally.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.170
Now, I will logout as
Charko and login as John

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:12.720
and do the same thing.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:14.490
However, John will
create an instance

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:17.279
in the production project
for which he is the owner.

00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:29.680
When all that is done, I will
pin the development instance

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:32.740
from the production instance
using the Shared VPC

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.790
internal IP address to
confirm I have connectivity

00:04:36.790 --> 00:04:39.460
and the Shared VPC is working.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.210
There you have it.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.320
Simple and easy.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.090
And Mary has all the
control she needs

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.460
to give the appropriate
engineers access

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:47.470
to the right
networking resources.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.630
LORIN PRICE: Life is amazing.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.090
The network administrators
have complete control

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:53.560
over the network
and no longer need

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:55.330
to worry about any
network changes that

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:56.980
were made by the developers.

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.980
This lets the developers focus
more on what they're best at

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.720
and helps me to
relax a bit more.

00:05:01.720 --> 00:05:03.160
If you enjoyed
today's demo, don't

00:05:03.160 --> 00:05:05.527
forget to like,
comment, and subscribe.

00:05:05.527 --> 00:05:08.110
GUSTAVO MANTOVAN: And if you'd
like to get in contact with us,

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:10.120
click on the link
in the description.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.410
Thanks for watching.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:13.560
[MUSIC PLAYING]

